WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.642
Coding Exercise 2 changes the population rule.

00:00:03.642 --> 00:00:09.027
This time, every patient must appear, even when the patient has no admission.

00:00:09.027 --> 00:00:13.797
The phrase every patient tells you which table must be preserved.

00:00:13.797 --> 00:00:17.037
Patients should be on the left side of a LEFT JOIN, while admissions is optional.

00:00:17.037 --> 00:00:23.627
Before running the query, predict what an unmatched patient should look like.

00:00:23.627 --> 00:00:30.017
The patient ID and name should still have values, while admission ID and diagnosis should be NULL.

00:00:30.017 --> 00:00:35.217
Also remember that LEFT JOIN does not automatically create one row per patient.

00:00:35.217 --> 00:00:39.607
A patient with several admissions can still appear several times.

00:00:39.607 --> 00:00:42.697
Preservation and grain are different concepts.

00:00:42.697 --> 00:00:45.662
Use Run and Check after you have written the join.

00:00:45.662 --> 00:00:51.102
If the unmatched patient disappears, examine whether you accidentally used INNER JOIN or added a filter that

00:00:51.102 --> 00:00:54.359
removes NULL admission rows.
